#: ../eduwifi-watchdog.sh:62
msgid ""
"Usage: %s [command] [options]\n"
"\n"
"Commands:\n"
"  check        Check the Wi-Fi and recover it if needed (default; used by "
"the timer)\n"
"  status       Show Wi-Fi and watchdog status plus the latest events\n"
"  disconnect   Disconnect the Wi-Fi manually; the watchdog will not "
"reconnect until \"on\"\n"
"  off          Turn the Wi-Fi radio off; stays off (even after reboot) until "
"\"on\"\n"
"  on           Turn the Wi-Fi on, re-enable autoconnect and connect to the "
"networks\n"
"  test         Simulate a driver hang and verify the watchdog recovers it "
"(root)\n"
"  gui [ACTION] Desktop dialog used by the menu entry; ACTION is status, off, "
"on or recover\n"
"\n"
"Options for \"check\":\n"
"  --dry-run    Only report what would be done, change nothing\n"
"  --force      Skip straight to reloading the kernel module\n"
"\n"
"Configuration: %s"
msgstr ""

